<section class="dotfiles landing-feature" aria-labelledby="dotfiles-title">
  <div class="dotfiles__copy">
    <h2 id="dotfiles-title">Your setup, <span class="dotfiles__highlight">in one file.</span></h2>
    <p>Settings, aliases, shortcuts, job switches, and the default AI model live in <code>~/.config/nevermind/config.json</code>. Commit it, symlink it, or copy it to a new Mac.</p>
    <p>A palette change counts as applied only after it is saved. Edit the file and Nevermind applies the change within a second.</p>
    <ul class="dotfiles__notes">
      <li>A broken or deleted file blocks saving. Palette changes show an error, and the file is left as you wrote it.</li>
      <li>Shortcuts and aliases for AI-generated extensions stay on this Mac, as do chats, clipboard history, recents, and extension data.</li>
      <li>A shortcut that another action or macOS already uses shows as Not active, with the reason, instead of failing silently.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="dotfiles__files" aria-label="Example config.json with settings, an alias, a custom shortcut, a disabled shortcut, a disabled job, and the default AI model">
    <div class="dotfiles__path">~/.config/nevermind/config.json</div>
    <pre><code>{`{
  "version": 1,
  "settings": {
    "paletteHotkey": "Command+Alt+K",
    "showClipboardInRoot": false
  },
  "aliases": {
    "extension-action:my-tools:open-notes": ["notes", "journal"]
  },
  "shortcuts": {
    "extension-action:my-tools:open-notes": "Command+Shift+N",
    "extension-action:calendar:next-meeting": null
  },
  "jobs": {
    "enabled": { "cache.thumbnails": false }
  },
  "ai": {
    "defaultModel": "smart"
  }
}`}</code></pre>
    <p class="dotfiles__caption"><code>null</code> turns off a shortcut that an extension declares.</p>
  </div>
</section>

